# Copy to .env (ignored). Names only; never commit a value.

# The keystore account name and its PUBLIC address. No private key anywhere, ever.
DEPLOYER_ACCOUNT=default
DEPLOYER=0x0000000000000000000000000000000000000000

# Optional. A keyless public endpoint is the default; uncomment and set a provider URL for reliability.
# (Leave it commented rather than empty: an empty value would override the default.)
# SEPOLIA_RPC_URL=https://

# Optional. Source verification on Etherscan; Sourcify needs no key. Same rule: comment, do not blank.
# ETHERSCAN_API_KEY=

# OPTIONAL, and not required by any current workflow. Measured 2026-09-10: Robinhood's testnet
# Blockscout explorer answered read-only calls without a key on all three per-instance surfaces —
# the REST API, the Etherscan-compatible API, and /api/eth-rpc. Blockscout's documentation states a
# valid key can increase RPS; keys come from Blockscout's account system. No keyed rate limit was
# measured, so none is claimed. Set it with `make scan-key`, which prompts silently and writes only
# to .env — never as a command argument.
# ROBINHOOD_SCAN_API_KEY=
